---
title: Nested data and object arrays
description: Submit a nested object with an editable array of objects using JSON submission, Fieldset and indexed ElementField names.
---

<script>
	import { Callout } from "$lib/markdown";
</script>

A native HTML form can only send flat, repeated input names — it cannot express `contacts[0].email`. Superforms solves this with `dataType: "json"`, which serializes the `$formData` store instead of the DOM, so any nesting your schema defines round-trips exactly.

## Schema

```ts title="src/routes/contacts/schema.ts"
import { z } from "zod/v3";

export const contactsSchema = z.object({
	profile: z.object({ name: z.string().min(2, "Enter at least two characters.") }),
	contacts: z
		.array(z.object({ email: z.string().email("Enter a valid email address.") }))
		.min(1),
});

export type ContactsData = z.infer<typeof contactsSchema>;
```

## Server

```ts title="src/routes/contacts/+page.server.ts"
import { fail } from "@sveltejs/kit";
import { superValidate } from "sveltekit-superforms";
import { zod } from "sveltekit-superforms/adapters";
import { contactsSchema } from "./schema.js";

export const load = async () => ({
	form: await superValidate(
		{
			profile: { name: "Ada" },
			contacts: [{ email: "a@example.com" }, { email: "b@example.com" }],
		},
		zod(contactsSchema)
	),
});

export const actions = {
	default: async ({ request }) => {
		const form = await superValidate(request, zod(contactsSchema));
		return form.valid ? { form } : fail(400, { form });
	},
};
```

## Form

`Field` points at the nested scalar `profile.name`. The `contacts` array gets a `Fieldset`, and each row's scalar gets an `ElementField` whose name is the indexed path. The `as` cast on the name keeps Superforms' template-literal path types happy while `index` stays a plain `number` at runtime.

```svelte title="src/routes/contacts/+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { untrack } from "svelte";
	import { superForm, type SuperValidated } from "sveltekit-superforms";
	import { Control, ElementField, Field, Fieldset, Label, Legend } from "@emmorts/formsnap";
	import type { ContactsData } from "./schema.js";

	let { data }: { data: { form: SuperValidated<ContactsData> } } = $props();

	const form = superForm(
		untrack(() => data.form),
		{ dataType: "json", resetForm: false }
	);
	const { form: formData, enhance } = form;

	// Superforms can replace row objects during taint updates, so object identity is not a
	// stable key. Keep a separate list of ids, initialized once from the initial row count.
	const initialRowCount = untrack(() => data.form.data.contacts.length);
	let rowIds = $state(Array.from({ length: initialRowCount }, (_, index) => index));
	let nextRowId = initialRowCount;

	function addRow() {
		rowIds = [...rowIds, nextRowId++];
		$formData.contacts = [...$formData.contacts, { email: "" }];
	}

	function removeRow() {
		rowIds = rowIds.slice(0, -1);
		$formData.contacts = $formData.contacts.slice(0, -1);
	}
</script>

<form method="POST" use:enhance>
	<Field {form} name="profile.name" fieldErrors>
		<Control>
			{#snippet children({ props })}
				<Label>Profile name</Label>
				<input {...props} bind:value={$formData.profile.name} />
			{/snippet}
		</Control>
	</Field>

	<Fieldset {form} name="contacts" fieldErrors>
		<Legend>Contacts</Legend>
		{#each $formData.contacts as _, index (rowIds[index])}
			<ElementField
				{form}
				name={`contacts[${index}].email` as `contacts[${number}].email`}
				fieldErrors
			>
				<Control>
					{#snippet children({ props })}
						<Label>Contact {index + 1}</Label>
						<input {...props} bind:value={$formData.contacts[index].email} />
					{/snippet}
				</Control>
			</ElementField>
		{/each}
	</Fieldset>

	<button type="button" onclick={addRow}>Add row</button>
	<button type="button" onclick={removeRow}>Remove row</button>
	<button type="submit">Save contacts</button>
</form>
```

## How it works

- `dataType: "json"` makes `use:enhance` submit the serialized `$formData` store, so the server receives the nested structure exactly as the schema declares it.
- Every control binds to `$formData` (not a local variable), keeping the store the single source of truth that gets serialized.
- `Fieldset` groups the array and provides the parent context each `ElementField` requires — an `ElementField` must sit inside a `Field` or `Fieldset`.
- The indexed name `contacts[N].email` resolves errors per row, so `fieldErrors` on each `ElementField` renders only that row's messages, while `fieldErrors` on the `Fieldset` surfaces array-level errors like the `min(1)` violation.
- Row keys come from `rowIds`, a list you own; mutate it together with `$formData.contacts` on every add, remove or reorder so the `{#each}` block keeps DOM nodes matched to rows.

<Callout type="warning">

JSON submission requires JavaScript — `use:enhance` is not optional here. A native POST without it sends repeated flat names that cannot express the nested paths. If the form must work unenhanced, use [primitive arrays](/docs/recipes/primitive-arrays) with a flat schema instead.

</Callout>

<Callout type="note">

Keep the `nextRowId` counter separate from array indexes. Reusing an index as a key after a removal collides with a surviving row's key and Svelte reuses the wrong DOM node, scrambling bindings and focus.

</Callout>
